window.CURRENT_TASK={"task_id": "L1-FUC-011-A2", "layer": "L1", "target_id": "FUC-011", "artifact_id": "FUC-011-A2", "title": "FUC-011 Transfer Reporting Responsibility / A2", "protocol_version": "L1_final_semantic_verified_candidate_v2", "artifact_sha256": "50f53f48f8709c791fe4285ea466011af6c59723ce7e6bbe342c35359d9a9602", "source_sha256": "40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99", "reference_sha256": null, "reference_origin": null, "instructions": "<pre>只依据本断言允许且实际提供的引用证据的并集判断，不使用其他页面或常识补充。entailment=所有实质内容获支持；contradiction=直接矛盾；neutral=有实质内容无支持且不矛盾。槽位适配独立判断。无合法引用填写 NO_VALID_CITATION，不得猜测支持。保留审计候选断言原边界，不用最终槽位代替。</pre>", "material_html": "<h3>Transfer Reporting Responsibility</h3><p>给定参与者：C2 JU</p><p>按逐断言所列证据作答。最终槽位仅用于组织者计算 ESC；不替代审计候选。</p>", "groups": [{"key": "claims", "title": "逐断言评价", "fields": [{"key": "citation", "label": "引用状态", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["VALID", "NO_VALID_CITATION", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "entailment", "label": "来源蕴含", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["entailment", "contradiction", "neutral", "NO_VALID_CITATION", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "slot_fit", "label": "槽位适配", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["true", "false", "NOT_EVALUATED", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "reason", "label": "证据判断理由", "type": "textarea", "required": true}, {"key": "slot_reason", "label": "槽位判断理由", "type": "textarea", "required": true}], "rows": [{"title": "goal:0", "html": "<pre>To transfer reporting responsibility (R^2) for a track by having a C2 JU relinquish or assume R^2 in accordance with the applicable R^2 rules.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277, milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215, milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277, milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215, milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215</h4><pre>d. Track reporting procedures when entering, departing, and reentering the interface.\nEach $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU has the responsibility to determine whether the data points being detected by its local sensors are currently reported on the interface and if there are any conflicts between locally derived information and information reported on the interface. To accomplish this, each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU must continuously correlate locally derived ballistic missile tracks with ballistic missile tracks reported on the Surveillance NPG. Each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU shall report on all uncorrelated local ballistic missile tracks and shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for those tracks in accordance with the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules as specified in paragraph 4.4.6.15.</pre><p>原始页位置：[68]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:0", "html": "<pre>For air, surface, or land tracks, the C2 JU is capable of assuming R^2 for the track.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:1", "html": "<pre>For air, surface, or land tracks, the C2 JU has initially achieved Active status or has returned to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:2", "html": "<pre>For air, surface, or land tracks, sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed before transmitting the tracks.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:3", "html": "<pre>For air and surface tracks, the minimum wait before transmitting tracks is 12 seconds; for land tracks, the minimum wait before transmitting tracks is 48 seconds.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "trigger:0", "html": "<pre>The use case is initiated when a C2 JU receives a remote track report in which remote TQ is greater than the local TQ, or receives a remote track report for the track which contains a TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose STN is greater than the local STN, for a real-time Air, Surface (Maritime) or Land (Ground) track.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P52#C175；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P52#C175</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P52#C175</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for a real-time Air, Surface (Maritime) or Land (Ground) track upon reception of a remote track report in which remote TQ is greater than the local TQ, or upon reception of a remote track report for the track which contains a TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose STN is greater than the local STN.\nj. A JU with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\n4.4.4.15 INFORMATION DIFFERENCE RECOGNITION AND RESOLUTION\nThe exchange of Air, Surface (Maritime),</pre><p>原始页位置：[52]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:0", "html": "<pre>C2 JU receives a remote track report for a real-time track.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:1", "html": "<pre>C2 JU receives a remote track report with TQ greater than the local TQ for a real-time track.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:2", "html": "<pre>Upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than the local TQ, the C2 JU relinquishes R^2 for the real-time track.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:3", "html": "<pre>After applying all the applicable rules, upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN, the C2 JU relinquishes R^2 for the real-time track.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:4", "html": "<pre>A C2 JU with R^2 retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the rules or until the track is dropped.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:5", "html": "<pre>Common tracking shares a common track number and shifts R^2 between C2 JUs; each air, surface (maritime), land (ground), and space tracked object is normally reported by one C2 JU while other C2 JUs withhold their reports.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68</h4><pre>4.4.4.3 COMMON TRACKING\na. Common tracking is defined as sharing of a common track number and shifting $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ between $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs. Each air, surface (maritime), land (ground), and space tracked object normally will be reported by one $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU while other $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs withhold their reports to prevent cluttering the tactical plot. Determination of the $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU responsible for reporting the tracked object shall be in accordance with the procedures in the Air, Surface, Land, and Space Surveillance sections. In this section and in section 4.7.3, Resolution of Air and Surface Track Dual Designations,</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:6", "html": "<pre>For air, surface, or land tracks, C2 JUs capable of assuming R^2 shall not transmit tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed; the minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:0", "html": "<pre>For Subsurface tracks, it is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs; the first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number, and no other JU shall report the contact using that track number unless one of the specified conditions occurs, including receipt of a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</h4><pre>4.4.5.10 SUBSURFACE TRACK REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY\nSubsurface track reporting responsibility procedures are different from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks. It is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs. This is to ensure continuity of reporting when contact is frequently lost/regained, and to allow comparison of different JUs&#x27; data to localize and identify contacts. The following are the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules for Subsurface tracks:\na. The first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number. No other JU shall report the contact using that track number, unless one of the following occurs:\n(1) A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received containing the TN.\n(2) A J3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:1", "html": "<pre>If a locally derived ballistic missile track is uncorrelated with ballistic missile tracks reported on the Surveillance NPG, the C2 JU shall report on the uncorrelated local ballistic missile track and shall assume R^2 for that track in accordance with the R^2 rules.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215</h4><pre>d. Track reporting procedures when entering, departing, and reentering the interface.\nEach $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU has the responsibility to determine whether the data points being detected by its local sensors are currently reported on the interface and if there are any conflicts between locally derived information and information reported on the interface. To accomplish this, each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU must continuously correlate locally derived ballistic missile tracks with ballistic missile tracks reported on the Surveillance NPG. Each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU shall report on all uncorrelated local ballistic missile tracks and shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for those tracks in accordance with the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules as specified in paragraph 4.4.6.15.</pre><p>原始页位置：[68]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:2", "html": "<pre>If the received remote track report does not cause relinquishment under the applicable TQ or Source TN rules, the C2 JU with R^2 retains responsibility for the real-time track until it is relinquished in accordance with the rules or until the track is dropped.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:3", "html": "<pre>If the track is a ballistic missile track, a unit assuming R^2 for the ballistic missile track need not assume R^2 for the associated launch point; the unit no longer holding R^2 on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:4", "html": "<pre>If IFF/SIF surveillance data are involved, the JU with R^2 reports all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that track in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages; JUs without R^2 monitor such data and only report if they hold different data with the J7.5 message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154, milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154, milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154</h4><pre>4.4.4.9.1 IFF/SIF SURVEILLANCE DATA REPORTING\nThe reporting of IFF/SIF surveillance data in the J3.2C1 and J3.3C1 words for\nAir and Surface tracks, respectively, is the responsibility of the JU with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$\nwhile all other JUs without $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ are responsible for monitoring such data and\nonly reporting if they hold different data with the J7.5 message. In this\nway the JU with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ can be assumed to be reporting the most current data\navailable in the interface. Surveillance reporting rules are as follows:\na. $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ units shall report all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that\ntrack in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages. Validity of</pre><p>原始页位置：[47]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395</h4><pre>6 IFF/SIF DATA MANAGEMENT AND SPECIAL CODE REPORTING\nManagement of IFF/SIF data is required to insure commonality of data between the IUs. The J7.5 message with the following action values is used to perform this function:\na. J7.5 (ACT = 0) Clear IFF/SIF message.\nb. J7.5 (ACT = 1) IFF/SIF Difference Report message.\nc. J7.5 (ACT = 2) IFF/SIF Update Request message.\nd. J7.5 (ACT = 3) Special Code message.\nThe reporting of IFF/SIF data in conjunction with periodic surveillance data is the responsibility of the JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;, while all other JUs without R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; are responsible for monitoring such data and only reporting different data with the J7.5 message. In this way the JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; can be assumed to be reporting the most current data available on the interface.</pre><p>原始页位置：[118]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:5", "html": "<pre>If the C2 JU assumes R^2 for a track, the J3.XC1 message is transmitted only by the JU with R^2, at the next opportunity for new tracks when assuming R^2 or when data changes.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146</h4><pre>The table defines functional behaviors for specific message types across five operational categories: Surveillance Data Reporting, Difference Resolution, Data Updating, and Clearing IFF/SIF Data. Each row corresponds to a distinct message or action, with its associated behavior in each category.\n\n1. **Message: PPLI J2.0C1, J2.2C1, J2.3C1, J2.4C1 IUs — OWN UNIT IFF/SIF DATA**\n   - *Surveillance Data Reporting*: Transmitted periodically with the J2.XB message.\n   - *Difference Resolution*: Not applicable (NA).\n   - *Data Updating*: Not applicable (NA).\n   - *Clearing IFF/SIF Data*: Not applicable (NA).\n\n2. **Message: J3.XC1 — TRANSMITTED ONLY BY JU WITH R²**\n   - *Surveillance Data Reporting*: \n     - Transmitted at next opportunity for new tracks when assuming R² or when data changes.</pre><p>原始页位置：[46]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:6", "html": "<pre>For air, surface, or land tracks, the minimum wait before transmitting tracks may be either an automatic or a manual function.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:7", "html": "<pre>If a C2 JU is deactivating a receive filter, the minimum wait before reporting air, surface, or land tracks also applies.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:0", "html": "<pre>1. If a C^2 JU capable of assuming R^2 for air, surface, or land tracks has not completed sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration, or the minimum wait has not elapsed (12 seconds for air and surface tracks; 48 seconds for land tracks), the C^2 JU shall not transmit those tracks; Exit: track transmission is deferred until the checks and minimum wait are satisfied.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:1", "html": "<pre>2. If a J3.7 message is transmitted by a non-R^2 JU with the Response Indicator set to value 1, it shall not affect reporting responsibility; Exit: reporting responsibility remains unchanged.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290</h4><pre>J3.7 message. J3.7 messages transmitted by nonR&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs with the Response Indicator set to value 1 shall not affect reporting responsibility.\n4.4.7.3 TIME DATA\nThe J3.7I word contains the time the EW product information reported on the interface was valid; time is expressed in hours, minutes, and seconds.\n4.4.7.4 ELECTRONIC WARFARE INFORMATION MANAGEMENT\nUpon receipt of a J7.1 (ACT = 1) message or upon receipt of a J7.1 (ACT = 0) message with an EA, ES, or EW Fixes Data Request Indicator set, addressed JUs shall respond as follows (see also paragraph 4.7.2.1.5 and Table 4.7-4):\na. If the J7.1 Addressee TN is set to value 00177, JUs with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; transmit all J3.7 EW data on the TN or as specified by the Request Indicator set to value 1.\nb. If the J7.</pre><p>原始页位置：[86]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:2", "html": "<pre>3. For Subsurface tracks, if a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN is received, the prohibition on another JU reporting the contact using that track number is lifted; Exit: another JU may report the contact using that track number under the stated drop-track condition.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</h4><pre>4.4.5.10 SUBSURFACE TRACK REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY\nSubsurface track reporting responsibility procedures are different from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks. It is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs. This is to ensure continuity of reporting when contact is frequently lost/regained, and to allow comparison of different JUs&#x27; data to localize and identify contacts. The following are the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules for Subsurface tracks:\na. The first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number. No other JU shall report the contact using that track number, unless one of the following occurs:\n(1) A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received containing the TN.\n(2) A J3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:3", "html": "<pre>4. For an emergency point, if a J7.0 (ACT = 0) message is received, the unit with R^2 is declared inactive, or no periodic update is received for three consecutive update intervals, another JU may, by operator action only, assume R^2 for the point; Exit: the assuming JU shall use the same TN Reference and the same value of TN Previously Reported as those reported by the previous reporting unit, and the latest JU to report the point has R^2.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55</h4><pre>4.4.3.2.2 REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY FOR EMERGENCY POINTS\nAny JU may report, through operator action onl $. \\ y ,$ on a previously reported emergency point when that JU has additional or more current information on the point. In addition, if a J7.0 (ACT = 0) message is received on an emergency point, the unit with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ is declared inactive, or if no periodic update is received for three consecutive update intervals, another JU may, by operator action only, assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for the point. A JU assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for an emergency point shall use the same TN Reference and the same value of TN Previously Reported as those reported by the previous reporting unit. The latest JU to report a point has $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for that point.\n4.4.3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[20]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:4", "html": "<pre>5. If a J2 PPLI message is not received for 40 to 60 seconds, or a J2 PPLI message other than J2.0 is received with the NPS Indicator set to Inactive or Conditional Radio Silence, or a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received from the FJU for a PU, RU, or other IU, a C^2 JU shall assume R^2 of an IU in accordance with the reporting rules for a real-time track if the C^2 JU has correlated local sensor data; Exit: the C^2 JU assumes R^2 for the IU.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20</h4><pre>The PPLI Track Number and Identity Indicator field and the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator field shall both be reported as No Statement.\n4.4.2.2.2 REPORTING OF INACTIVE AND LIMITED STATUS INTERFACE UNITS\nA $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU shall assume $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ of an IU (including $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ and nonC&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs and forwarded PUs and RUs) in accordance with the reporting rules for a real-time track if the $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU has correlated local sensor data, when:\na. A J2 PPLI message is not received for 40 to 60 seconds, or\nb. A J2 PPLI message, other than J2.0, is received with the NPS Indicator set to Inactive or Conditional Radio Silence, or\nc. A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received from the FJU for a PU, RU, or other IU, or\nd.</pre><p>原始页位置：[8]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:5", "html": "<pre>6. If the track is dropped, the JU with R^2 does not retain responsibility beyond the drop; Exit: R^2 retention for that track ends when the track is dropped.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:6", "html": "<pre>7. If a J3.5 (PTI = 0) message is received, Course and Speed shall be set to No Statement, the Track Quality field shall be set to 0, and Course, Speed, and Track Quality shall not be processed; Exit: those fields from the J3.5 (PTI = 0) message are not processed.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53</h4><pre>Course and Speed shall be set to No Statement in a J3.5 (PTI = 0) message. The J3.5 (PTI = 0) Track Quality field shall be set to 0. Course, Speed, and Track Quality shall not be processed upon receipt of a J3.5 (PTI = 0) message.\n4.4.3.2 REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY FOR POINTS, LINES, AND AREAS\nThe following subparagraphs amplify the general $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules specified in paragraph 4.4.2.2. Both the general rules and the amplification of those rules for points, lines, and areas, detailed below, shall be followed.\n4.4.3.2.1 REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY FOR REFERENCE POINTS, LINES, AND AREAS AND GROUND POINTS\nThe originator of a J3.0 or J3.5 (PTI = 0) point, line, or area retains $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ as long as the originator remains active and reports the point, line, or area.</pre><p>原始页位置：[19]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:0", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU has relinquished R^2 for the real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than the local TQ.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:1", "html": "<pre>After applying all the above rules, the C2 JU has relinquished R^2 for the real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277</h4><pre>A JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than local TQ.\ni. A JU with R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on a track retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the above rules or until the track is dropped.\nj. After applying all the above rules, a JU relinquishes R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a realtime track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.\nk. A unit assuming R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for a ballistic missile track need not assume R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; for the associated launch point. The unit no longer holding R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.\n4.4.6.</pre><p>原始页位置：[81]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:2", "html": "<pre>When a locally derived ballistic missile track is uncorrelated with ballistic missile tracks reported on the Surveillance NPG, the C2 JU has reported on the uncorrelated local ballistic missile track and has assumed R^2 for that track in accordance with the R^2 rules.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215</h4><pre>d. Track reporting procedures when entering, departing, and reentering the interface.\nEach $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU has the responsibility to determine whether the data points being detected by its local sensors are currently reported on the interface and if there are any conflicts between locally derived information and information reported on the interface. To accomplish this, each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU must continuously correlate locally derived ballistic missile tracks with ballistic missile tracks reported on the Surveillance NPG. Each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU shall report on all uncorrelated local ballistic missile tracks and shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for those tracks in accordance with the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules as specified in paragraph 4.4.6.15.</pre><p>原始页位置：[68]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:3", "html": "<pre>For an emergency point, a JU assuming R^2 shall use the same TN Reference and the same value of TN Previously Reported as those reported by the previous reporting unit.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55</h4><pre>4.4.3.2.2 REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY FOR EMERGENCY POINTS\nAny JU may report, through operator action onl $. \\ y ,$ on a previously reported emergency point when that JU has additional or more current information on the point. In addition, if a J7.0 (ACT = 0) message is received on an emergency point, the unit with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ is declared inactive, or if no periodic update is received for three consecutive update intervals, another JU may, by operator action only, assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for the point. A JU assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for an emergency point shall use the same TN Reference and the same value of TN Previously Reported as those reported by the previous reporting unit. The latest JU to report a point has $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for that point.\n4.4.3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[20]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:4", "html": "<pre>For an emergency point, the latest JU to report the point has R^2.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55</h4><pre>4.4.3.2.2 REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY FOR EMERGENCY POINTS\nAny JU may report, through operator action onl $. \\ y ,$ on a previously reported emergency point when that JU has additional or more current information on the point. In addition, if a J7.0 (ACT = 0) message is received on an emergency point, the unit with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ is declared inactive, or if no periodic update is received for three consecutive update intervals, another JU may, by operator action only, assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for the point. A JU assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for an emergency point shall use the same TN Reference and the same value of TN Previously Reported as those reported by the previous reporting unit. The latest JU to report a point has $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for that point.\n4.4.3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[20]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:5", "html": "<pre>For Subsurface tracks, the first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</h4><pre>4.4.5.10 SUBSURFACE TRACK REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY\nSubsurface track reporting responsibility procedures are different from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks. It is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs. This is to ensure continuity of reporting when contact is frequently lost/regained, and to allow comparison of different JUs&#x27; data to localize and identify contacts. The following are the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules for Subsurface tracks:\na. The first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number. No other JU shall report the contact using that track number, unless one of the following occurs:\n(1) A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received containing the TN.\n(2) A J3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}], "repeat": false, "min_rows": 0}], "blockers": [], "claim_meta": [{"slot": "goal", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "To transfer reporting responsibility (R^2) for a track by having a C2 JU relinquish or assume R^2 in accordance with the applicable R^2 rules.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P108#C368", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "For air, surface, or land tracks, the C2 JU is capable of assuming R^2 for the track.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P24#C67", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20", "milstd6016b_sec4:P101#C339", "milstd6016b_sec4:P124#C418"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "For air, surface, or land tracks, the C2 JU has initially achieved Active status or has returned to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P24#C67", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20", "milstd6016b_sec4:P101#C339", "milstd6016b_sec4:P124#C418"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "For air, surface, or land tracks, sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed before transmitting the tracks.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P24#C67", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20", "milstd6016b_sec4:P101#C339", "milstd6016b_sec4:P124#C418"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "For air and surface tracks, the minimum wait before transmitting tracks is 12 seconds; for land tracks, the minimum wait before transmitting tracks is 48 seconds.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P24#C67", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20", "milstd6016b_sec4:P101#C339", "milstd6016b_sec4:P124#C418"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "trigger", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "The use case is initiated when a C2 JU receives a remote track report in which remote TQ is greater than the local TQ, or receives a remote track report for the track which contains a TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose STN is greater than the local STN, for a real-time Air, Surface (Maritime) or Land (Ground) track.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P52#C175"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C148", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P52#C175", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "C2 JU receives a remote track report for a real-time track.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "C2 JU receives a remote track report with TQ greater than the local TQ for a real-time track.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "Upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than the local TQ, the C2 JU relinquishes R^2 for the real-time track.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "After applying all the applicable rules, upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN, the C2 JU relinquishes R^2 for the real-time track.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "A C2 JU with R^2 retains the responsibility until it is relinquished in accordance with the rules or until the track is dropped.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "Common tracking shares a common track number and shifts R^2 between C2 JUs; each air, surface (maritime), land (ground), and space tracked object is normally reported by one C2 JU while other C2 JUs withhold their reports.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 6, "content": "For air, surface, or land tracks, C2 JUs capable of assuming R^2 shall not transmit tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed; the minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "For Subsurface tracks, it is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs; the first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number, and no other JU shall report the contact using that track number unless one of the specified conditions occurs, including receipt of a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "If a locally derived ballistic missile track is uncorrelated with ballistic missile tracks reported on the Surveillance NPG, the C2 JU shall report on the uncorrelated local ballistic missile track and shall assume R^2 for that track in accordance with the R^2 rules.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "If the received remote track report does not cause relinquishment under the applicable TQ or Source TN rules, the C2 JU with R^2 retains responsibility for the real-time track until it is relinquished in accordance with the rules or until the track is dropped.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "If the track is a ballistic missile track, a unit assuming R^2 for the ballistic missile track need not assume R^2 for the associated launch point; the unit no longer holding R^2 on the ballistic missile track may continue to report the launch point in accordance with the transmit/receive rules.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "If IFF/SIF surveillance data are involved, the JU with R^2 reports all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that track in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages; JUs without R^2 monitor such data and only report if they hold different data with the J7.5 message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "If the C2 JU assumes R^2 for a track, the J3.XC1 message is transmitted only by the JU with R^2, at the next opportunity for new tracks when assuming R^2 or when data changes.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 6, "content": "For air, surface, or land tracks, the minimum wait before transmitting tracks may be either an automatic or a manual function.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 7, "content": "If a C2 JU is deactivating a receive filter, the minimum wait before reporting air, surface, or land tracks also applies.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P118#C395", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "1. If a C^2 JU capable of assuming R^2 for air, surface, or land tracks has not completed sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration, or the minimum wait has not elapsed (12 seconds for air and surface tracks; 48 seconds for land tracks), the C^2 JU shall not transmit those tracks; Exit: track transmission is deferred until the checks and minimum wait are satisfied.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "2. If a J3.7 message is transmitted by a non-R^2 JU with the Response Indicator set to value 1, it shall not affect reporting responsibility; Exit: reporting responsibility remains unchanged.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "3. For Subsurface tracks, if a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN is received, the prohibition on another JU reporting the contact using that track number is lifted; Exit: another JU may report the contact using that track number under the stated drop-track condition.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "4. For an emergency point, if a J7.0 (ACT = 0) message is received, the unit with R^2 is declared inactive, or no periodic update is received for three consecutive update intervals, another JU may, by operator action only, assume R^2 for the point; Exit: the assuming JU shall use the same TN Reference and the same value of TN Previously Reported as those reported by the previous reporting unit, and the latest JU to report the point has R^2.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "5. If a J2 PPLI message is not received for 40 to 60 seconds, or a J2 PPLI message other than J2.0 is received with the NPS Indicator set to Inactive or Conditional Radio Silence, or a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received from the FJU for a PU, RU, or other IU, a C^2 JU shall assume R^2 of an IU in accordance with the reporting rules for a real-time track if the C^2 JU has correlated local sensor data; Exit: the C^2 JU assumes R^2 for the IU.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "6. If the track is dropped, the JU with R^2 does not retain responsibility beyond the drop; Exit: R^2 retention for that track ends when the track is dropped.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 6, "content": "7. If a J3.5 (PTI = 0) message is received, Course and Speed shall be set to No Statement, the Track Quality field shall be set to 0, and Course, Speed, and Track Quality shall not be processed; Exit: those fields from the J3.5 (PTI = 0) message are not processed.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P86#C290", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C20"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "The C2 JU has relinquished R^2 for the real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ greater than the local TQ.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17", "milstd6016b_sec4:P80#C273", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "After applying all the above rules, the C2 JU has relinquished R^2 for the real-time track upon reception of a remote track report with TQ equal to the local TQ from a JU whose Source TN is greater than the local Source TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17", "milstd6016b_sec4:P80#C273", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "When a locally derived ballistic missile track is uncorrelated with ballistic missile tracks reported on the Surveillance NPG, the C2 JU has reported on the uncorrelated local ballistic missile track and has assumed R^2 for that track in accordance with the R^2 rules.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17", "milstd6016b_sec4:P80#C273", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "For an emergency point, a JU assuming R^2 shall use the same TN Reference and the same value of TN Previously Reported as those reported by the previous reporting unit.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17", "milstd6016b_sec4:P80#C273", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "For an emergency point, the latest JU to report the point has R^2.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17", "milstd6016b_sec4:P80#C273", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "For Subsurface tracks, the first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215", "milstd6016b_sec4:P19#C53", "milstd6016b_sec4:P83#C282", "milstd6016b_sec4:P20#C55", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P7#C17", "milstd6016b_sec4:P80#C273", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P81#C277"], "valid_citation": true}], "empty_slots": [], "material_sha256": "2109616b9417b93bd2b964c85aa0d2e475ac35ec9dff4fad8b6c1b4af7038e88"};
